<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--shiki-color-text)">  </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">&quot;message&quot;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-punctuation)">:</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-color-text)"> </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)">&quot;questions.refund.type: expected one of &#x27;noul&#x27;, &#x27;choice&#x27;, &#x27;score&#x27;&quot;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-punctuation)">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--shiki-color-text)">  </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">&quot;error_type&quot;</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-punctuation)">:</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-color-text)"> </span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string-expression)">&quot;invalid_request&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:var(--shiki-color-text)">}</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="my-4">Errors returned by the model provider are passed through unchanged, so a client that already handles TypeSafe errors keeps working.</p>
